<Base title="About — DRCA" active="about">
  <p class="eyebrow">About the DRCA</p>
  <h1>A civic association, since 1954.</h1>
  <p class="lede">The Del Ray Citizens Association (DRCA) is a non-profit 501(c)(4) organization for Del Ray
  residents and business owners in Alexandria, Virginia. We keep members informed on land use, public
  safety, schools, parks and recreation, transportation, housing, and the other issues that shape
  quality of life — and we represent the neighborhood before the Planning Commission, Board of Zoning
  Appeals, and City Council.</p>
  <p>The DRCA meets at <strong>7:00 pm on the second Wednesday of the month, September through June</strong>,
  typically via Zoom. Meeting details are shared in the member newsletter.</p>

  <h2>Why join?</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card"><h3>Stay informed</h3><p>Monthly meetings and newsletters cover land use, safety,
      transportation, volunteering, and events before they hit your feed.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Advocate</h3><p>The DRCA carries member positions into city forums — one letter
    from a thousand households lands differently than one from one.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Vote</h3><p>Members debate and decide DRCA positions — from restaurant patio
    expansions to zoning changes next to your alley.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Community</h3><p>The feel of Del Ray doesn't maintain itself. Dues fund the
    events that bring neighbors together.</p></div>
  </div>

